  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Murugan vs The District Collector on 8 January, 2024 Author: V.Bhavani Subbaroyan Bench: V.Bhavani Subbaroyan W.P(MD)No.3 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 08.01.2024 Coram The Honourable Mrs.Justice V.Bhavani Subbaroyan W.P(MD)No.336 of 2024 and W.M.P(MD)Nos.336 and 337 of 2024 Murugan ... -Vs- 1.The District Collector, Kanyakumari District, Kanyakumari. 2.The Block Development Officer, Thovalai Village Union, Kanyakumari District. 3.The Village President, Sagayanagar Village, Thovalai, Kanyakumari District. ... Res PRAYER:- Writ Petition is filed under Article 226 of the Constituti India, praying for the issuance of a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamu for the records relating to the impugned notice affixed by the thir respondent to seal the petitioner's shop situated at Shop No.1-37, Vellamadam Junction, Thovalai, Kanyakumari District and quash the s 1/8 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.P(MD) Murugan vs The District Collector on 8 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/91561510/ 1 and consequently direct the third respondent to consider the petiti application dated 08.08.2023 in pursuant to the order in W.P(MD)No. of 2023, dated 04.12.2023. For Petitioner : Mr.T.Palanisamy For Respondents : Mr.P.Thambidurai Govt. Advocate (for R1) Mr.C.Baskaran Govt. Advocate (for R2) Mr.Niranjan S.Kumar (for R3)",
    "facts": "In order to running the said shop, the petitioner has properly applied before the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India and obtained a registration certificate. The petitioner has entered into a lease agreement with the above said owner on 17.07.2020 and the rent was originally fixed at Rs.7,000/- per month. Thereafter, the shop owner has tried to evict the petitioner from the above shop forcibly without any proper reason. Hence, he filed a suit in O.S.No.49 of 2022 before the District Munsif-cum-Judicial Magistrate, Boothapandi and the same is pending. While so, at the instigation of the shop owner, the third respondent/Village President had sent a notice dated 21.07.2023 and 01.08.2023, seeking explanation for running the above shop without permission of the third respondent. However, the third respondent stated that there is no permission required for small shops. Further, the petitioner requested the third respondent to grant permission, if any permission is required for running broiler shop. While so, the third respondent has passed a resolution number 126, dated 08.08.2023, to seal the petitioner's shop, in the absence of the petitioner and without providing any opportunity to him. Hence, the petitioner filed a writ petition in W.P. (MD)No.28473 of 2023. After that the petitioner is in the legitimate expectation that the third respondent might have issued license to him for running the above said broiler shop.",
    "arguments": "4. The learned counsel appearing for the third respondent would submit that since the petitioners broiler shop creating health hazards to the local persons and a complaint has been received from the local persons, show cause notice has been issued and then only they proceeded further. He would further submit that the petitioner has been misusing the premises and all the wasted materials from the said business have been thrown out in the open space and there is a complaint from the local persons regarding this issue. Further, as per the rules and regulations of the local body, they have n o t o b t a i n e d a n y p e r m i s s i o n a s t h e a p p l i c a t i o n s e e k i n g p e r m i s s i o n i s s t i l l https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis pending."
  },
